  "term": "prophylaxis",
  "definition": "Prophylaxis is prevention: actions or programs designed to reduce risk, change factors that contribute to illness, or stop a disease from progressing. It can include therapeutic, nutritional, environmental, social, or behavioral measures used at individual or broader group levels.",
